1 0 0 1 60 760 Tm (Lecture 3: Linear Regression) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 736 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 60 712 Tm (A model predicts y from x with y = w*x + b.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 688 Tm (w is the weight \(slope\), b is the bias \(intercept\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 664 Tm (Example: w = 2, b = 1. For x = 3 the prediction is 2*3 + 1 = 7.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 640 Tm (Loss: the mean squared error between predictions and labels.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 616 Tm (MSE = \(1/n\) * sum_i \(y_i - yhat_i\)^2) Tj
ET
endstream
