1 0 0 1 60 760 Tm (Lecture 3: Gradient Descent) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 736 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 60 712 Tm (We update w by w <- w - lr * dL/dw.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 688 Tm (lr is the learning rate. A small lr is slow; a large lr may diverge.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 664 Tm (Example: w = 2, dL/dw = 4, lr = 0.1 gives w = 2 - 0.4 = 1.6.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 640 Tm (Repeat until the loss stops decreasing.) Tj
ET
